   "id": "dev-054",
   "kind": "Launch post",
   "draft": "1,200 repositories. 🤯\n\nWhen we launched Patchwork CI, we made a promise: always free for open source. Many people told us we were crazy. \"How will you make money?\" they asked.\n\nFast forward to today — we're running on 1,200 repositories, and about 900 of them are open source. 💚\n\nBut here's what truly blew my mind 👇\n\nAcross all those repos, 1 in 7 CI failures turned out to be a flaky test.\n\nLet that sink in. 1 in 7.\n\nThat's countless hours of developer time wasted on red builds that weren't real failures.\n\nOpen source didn't just give us users. It gave us data, feedback, and a community. In fact, our most-requested feature — GitLab support — came straight from OSS maintainers, and we shipped it on November 12. 🚀\n\nGiving back isn't charity. It's strategy.\n\n#OpenSource #DevOps #CI #DeveloperExperience #BuildInPublic",
