   "claude": "Patchwork CI now runs on 1,200 repositories.\n\nWhen we launched, we promised it would always be free for open source. Plenty of people told us that was crazy and asked how we planned to make money.\n\nToday about 900 of those 1,200 repositories are open source.\n\nThe number that surprised me most came from the builds themselves. Across all those repos, 1 in 7 CI failures turned out to be a flaky test. Each of those was a red build that wasn't a real failure, and developers lost hours chasing them.\n\nOpen source brought us users, and it also brought us data, feedback and a community. Our most-requested feature, GitLab support, came straight from OSS maintainers. We shipped it on November 12.\n\nGiving back to open source has been part of our strategy from the start.\n\n#OpenSource #DevOps #CI #DeveloperExperience #BuildInPublic",
